Example lifecycle code that could trigger a problem:

- Create a lifecycle in a content-type and try to console.log(ctx.state.user)

```js
  async beforeFindMany(event) {
    const ctx = strapi.requestContext.get();

    console.log(ctx.state.user);
  },
};
```

- In this case you would need to use `console.log(ctx?.state.user)` but ideally we should just temp disable all lifecycles during a transfer
